# The shell: top bar, status strip, config menu, motor picker, undo/redo, Simulate and Analyze frames.
# Run with the example rocket loaded: `cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/shell.drive out/shell`
viewport 1280x800
screenshot build.png

# Config menu opens upward over the foot of the parts bin.
click "CONFIG"
screenshot config-menu.png

# New configuration... opens the motor picker (mount-filtered, with the margin each motor would give).
click "New configuration…"
screenshot picker.png
click #motor-search
type "I284W"
click "I284W"
screenshot picker-selected.png
click "Add configuration"
screenshot config-added.png

# Undo and redo (top bar icon buttons) take the new configuration away and bring it back.
click "Undo"
screenshot undone.png
click "Redo"
screenshot redone.png

# A part added from the bin is one undo step too.
click "Body tube"
screenshot added-tube.png
click "Undo"
screenshot added-tube-undone.png

# The mode switch: Simulate and Analyze keep the top bar and status strip.
click "Simulate"
screenshot simulate.png
click "Analyze"
screenshot analyze.png
click "Build"
screenshot back-to-build.png
